WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 3 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:04.507
You are the fictional supervisor at Northstar Services.

00:00:04.747 --> 00:00:14.027
Your task is to review Avery Chen’s standard time sheet for the week of 5–9 October 2026, assignment NS-204.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:19.387
The training company uses task code DEL for delivery and TRN for training.

00:00:19.627 --> 00:00:22.869
These codes and review rules are invented for this sample.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:29.426
Before touching a decision control, establish worker, assignment, period, status, and your authority.

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:34.295
A familiar name is not enough: the same worker might have more than one assignment.

00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:38.973
Compare the sheet’s identifiers to the request and the approved assignment record.

00:00:39.213 --> 00:00:43.330
Open the detail record rather than deciding from an email subject.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:49.929
In SAP Fieldglass, submitted time sheets can be reached through Work Items or the Time Sheet list.

00:00:50.169 --> 00:00:54.713
Exact labels and available actions depend on role and configuration.

00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:59.305
This simulation asks for the review decision without connecting to Fieldglass.

00:00:59.995 --> 00:01:06.865
Worked example: TS-104 shows Avery, NS-204, 5–9 October, Submitted.

00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:13.633
TS-099 shows the same person and period but assignment NS-188.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:17.435
Select TS-104, then compare its daily lines.

00:01:17.675 --> 00:01:25.163
If you cannot establish approval authority, contact the designated program-office contact; do not borrow another account.

00:01:25.853 --> 00:01:26.941
Now it's your turn.

00:01:27.181 --> 00:01:29.549
Which record should you open for this request?

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.904
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

